odulus of $z$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"414e032253d59c9a8fdbcb5c","time_limit":25},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q03","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which identity always holds for the negation of a complex number $z$?","options":["$-z=\\overline z$ for all $z$","$-z=z^{-1}$ for all nonzero $z$","$-z=|z|$ for all $z$","$-(-z)=z$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"824ee72219a197e29722e67d","time_limit":25},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q04","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $-(1-\\mathrm{i})$?","options":["$1+\\mathrm{i}$","$-1+\\mathrm{i}$","$-1-\\mathrm{i}$","$1-\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9f4ab302b9afc57efb5ea37f","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q05","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $-(0+2\\mathrm{i})$?","options":["$0+2\\mathrm{i}$","$2+0\\mathrm{i}$","$0-2\\mathrm{i}$","$-2+0\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ca1c07d68ebbb8cb0794a929","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q06","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $z=3-4\\mathrm{i}$, what is $-z$?","options":["$3+4\\mathrm{i}$","$-3-4\\mathrm{i}$","$-3+4\\mathrm{i}$","$4-3\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"42399c9d989868f7a50acd64","time_limit":20},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q07","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How is $-z$ positioned geometrically relative to $z$?","options":["It is symmetric to $z$ about the origin.","It is the reflection of $z$ across the real axis.","It is the reflection of $z$ across the imaginary axis.","It has the same point as $z$ for every $z$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a427420e5f9019c838fe04f2","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q08","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which operation is easy to confuse with complex negation but is different?","options":["Complex conjugation","Complex addition","Writing a complex number in standard form","Adding zero"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ee434d7d09a7144749bc5fd4","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q09","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For which complex numbers is $-z=\\overline z$?","options":["Exactly when $z$ is real","Exactly when $z$ is purely imaginary","For all complex numbers","For no complex number"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6e3ea69a6b0a03df7d880bdd","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q10","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is $-(-2+5\\mathrm{i})$?","options":["$-2-5\\mathrm{i}$","$2+5\\mathrm{i}$","$-2+5\\mathrm{i}$","$2-5\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d5c779f37c1d9c3dc8564b4b","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q11","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which expression equals $z+(-z)$?","options":["$z$","$0_{\\mathbb C}$","$-z$","$2z$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8ff6db544dc7104dba78bfb9","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q12","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does the negation $-z$ of a complex number give?","options":["It gives the reflection across the real axis only.","It gives the additive inverse and the point symmetric about the origin.","It gives the reciprocal of every nonzero complex number.","It gives the distance from the origin."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e03a5d41c0f0b1b1ce205c56","time_limit":30},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q13","difficulty":"standard","q