?","options":["It changes only the imaginary coordinate.","It changes both coordinates while preserving distance from the origin.","It is undefined for real complex numbers.","It turns a number into its conjugate, flipping it across the real axis."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5fb3f73986acb0a316fd8a7a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q19","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $z=2+3\\mathrm{i}$ and $w=-z$, what is $z+w$?","options":["$4+6\\mathrm{i}$","$2-3\\mathrm{i}$","$0_{\\mathbb C}$","$-2-3\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4413b006c4d087fda73883ef","time_limit":40},{"id":"year-1-2a-math-iii-analysis-complex-negation-html-q20","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which pair consists of a complex number and its negation?","options":["$2-\\mathrm{i}$ and $2+\\mathrm{i}$","$2-\\mathrm{i}$ and $-2-\\mathrm{i}$","$2-\\mathrm{i}$ and $\\frac12+\\mathrm{i}$","$2-\\mathrm{i}$ and $-2+\\mathrm{i}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"220b3320c16f3a3ef2500a85","time_limit":40}]}}